  "notes": "These are common starting points rather than strict boundaries. Specialized chemistry and delivery can change which sites a modality reaches. The useful distinction is what is optimized and what establishes its function. Here, minibinder means a non-antibody protein binder. VHH and scFv belong to the antibody route even when they are physically small. The comparison is an author synthesis of documented tool scopes and experimental formats.\n\nSources\n[FDA] US FDA. Discovery and Development\nhttps://www.fda.gov/patients/drug-development-process/step-1-discovery-and-development\n\n[RF] Watson et al. De novo design of protein structure and function with RFdiffusion. Nature (2023)\nhttps://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06415-8\n\n[BINDCRAFT] Pacesa et al. One-shot design of functional protein binders with BindCraft. Nature (2025)\nhttps://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-025-09429-6\nhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12507698/\n\n[RFANTIBODY] Bennett et al. Atomically accurate de novo design of antibodies with RFdiffusion. Nature 649, 183–193 (2026), online 5 November 2025\nhttps://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-025-09721-5\nhttps://github.com/RosettaCommons/RFantibody\n\nSource check: 8 November 2026. Representative tools, not an exhaustive ranking."
